From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm exl3: decode windows on the 16-pair item plan

The two commits of ashhart/TensorFold PR #2044 (cbbac0273 the item plan,
610ce288b its GPU check at served size), taken from the PR branch as rebased
on upstream main 673a34b3b. The engine files apply to this stack unchanged;
only the three-line registration in zig/tests/cuda/main.zig is placed by hand,
because the neighbouring lines differ here.

A decode window's routed picks are grouped by the Router into items of up to
16 pairs, the grouped kernels run in their standard mode on that plan, and the
down epilogue writes the routed slot rows in place (no copy back). The bits
are the plain decode's: glm-exl3-items compares the two byte for byte.

Receipt on upstream main (docs/PR2044-AB.md, spark1-3, TP=3, drafts on):
decode +1.2 / +0.2 / +0.1 / +0.7 / +2.1% at 1 / 2 / 4 / 6 / 8 streams, every
reply digest equal to main's.

Receipt on this stack (spark1-3, TP=3, drafts on, knobs off; image
ai-engine:fix6 = the stack through 0042, ai-engine:fix7 = the same plus this
patch), tok/s at 1 / 2 / 4 / 6 / 8 streams, every reply digest equal:
  51.51 / 59.56 / 80.99 / 110.01 / 134.09 without
  52.02 / 60.26 / 82.67 / 113.29 / 137.01 with (+1.0 / +1.2 / +2.1 / +3.0 / +2.2%)
With TF_GLM_KDA_PAD=1 (the without row is the stack through 0041, which runs
the same code on these short prompts):
  63.94 / 74.66 / 93.28 / 124.59 / 150.80 without
  64.81 / 74.23 / 94.45 / 126.65 / 154.07 with (+1.4 / -0.6 / +1.3 / +1.7 / +2.2%)
The two-stream pad cell rerun in the order A B B A on fix6 and fix7 (means of
three rounds): 74.16, 75.02, 75.61, 74.37, so +1.4% with the patch and the
-0.6% cell was drift between boots.

